  "name": "jj (Jujutsu)",
  "description": "Jujutsu is a Git-compatible version control system designed for speed, correctness, and ease of history manipulation. It employs a working-copy-as-a-commit model where changes are automatically snapshotted, and it treats merge conflicts as first-class, evaluatable objects in its graph. The system features a functional revset language for commit selection, a robust operation log with built-in undo capabilities, and automatic propagation of rebases and conflict resolutions.",
